{
  "schema": "hnchain.conformance.core.state-tree",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "status": "stable",
  "status_meaning": "Promoted from \"draft\" to \"stable\": all promote_to_stable_when conditions are met as of ADR-0003 reaching Accepted (hn-state::key::OBJECT_ID_MAX_LEN = 64 bytes confirmed to still fit ADR-0003's decided 32-byte address_body). \"stable\" still only grades this vector set's coverage and curation, not a separate claim about the hn-smt-256-v1 math beyond what ADR-0005/ADR-0007/ADR-0003 already being Accepted already means.",
  "promote_to_stable_when": [],
  "depends_on": [
    "hnchain.adr.ADR-0003@accepted",
    "hnchain.adr.ADR-0005@accepted",
    "hnchain.adr.ADR-0007@accepted"
  ],
  "scope": {
    "included": [
      "state_key_core_derivation",
      "state_key_extension_derivation",
      "empty_hash_recursion",
      "leaf_and_internal_node_hashing",
      "state_root_computation",
      "update_order_independence"
    ],
    "excluded": [
      "raw_hash_algorithm_primitives",
      "account_value_binary_schema",
      "address_format_encoding",
      "proof_generation_and_verification",
      "storage_backend_behavior"
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "object_id values below are 32-byte opaque placeholders standing in for a canonical account address; ADR-0003 (Address Format, Accepted) fixes the address_body length at 32 bytes but not yet the exact derivation function, so these values are not derived the way a real address would be.",
    "value bytes below are opaque canonical payload placeholders standing in for a section or extension's HNCS-encoded value; the account state binary schema is not yet finalized and is out of scope for this vector set.",
    "object_id and subkey are bounded to 64 and 64 bytes respectively by the reference implementation; this is an implementation-level resource bound, not a consensus value."
  ],
  "params": {
    "object_id_max_len": 64,
    "subkey_max_len": 64,
    "domain_accounts": 1,
    "domain_account_extensions": 2
  },
